Simulations showing various stages in the development of converging-diverging (CD) nozzle choking. Each row shows the progression of the flow with time, with lines added in the adjacent column to clarify the observed flow geometry. The top row shows the initial development of characteristic lines and the formation of small boundary buffers. In the second row, the characteristic lines remain relatively stationary while the boundary buffers advance into the flow. In the final row, the upper and lower boundary buffers converge, restricting the available flow area and producing the observed choking behavior. 50,000 particles with 920 boundary particles, frame rate approximatly 1000 fps (1 spf), $v_x$=0.2, particle radius=0.1, dt=0.05.   
